# QueryShield — example environment configuration
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in real values for local development:
#   cp .env.example .env
# `.env` is git-ignored and must NEVER be committed. Everything below is a
# PLACEHOLDER — do not put real passwords, API keys, or production connection
# strings in THIS file.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What reads these (as of Phase 2)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The configuration system (`queryshield.load_config`) and the PostgreSQL
# adapter are implemented. They read the QUERYSHIELD_-prefixed variables below.
# The LLM (Mistral) and cache (Redis) are NOT implemented yet; those variables
# are documented here for later phases and are currently ignored.
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Naming & precedence (see docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-0017)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# * All settings use the prefix  QUERYSHIELD_
# * Nested settings use a double underscore  __  as the delimiter, e.g.
#   the `url` field of the `database` section is  QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__URL
# * Effective precedence, highest wins:
#       explicit overrides passed in code  >  environment variables  >
#       YAML config file  >  built-in safe defaults
# * Unknown QUERYSHIELD_ variables are ignored (so the test DSN below can
#   coexist with the app config without breaking startup).
# * Loading fails closed: a malformed or type-invalid security-relevant value
#   raises a structured ConfigError rather than being silently dropped.

# ---- Database (required) ----
# The only required setting. QueryShield expects to connect as a least-privilege
# role (see ADR-0002), not a superuser. Scheme must be postgresql:// (or
# postgres://). The value is held as a secret and never appears in logs, reprs,
# or error messages.
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__URL=postgresql://user:password@localhost:5432/queryshield

# ---- Database connection pool & timeouts (optional; safe defaults shown) ----
# Nothing deployment-specific is hard-coded; these all have overridable defaults.
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__POOL_MIN_SIZE=1
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__POOL_MAX_SIZE=10
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__POOL_TIMEOUT=30.0          # seconds to wait for a pooled conn
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__CONNECT_TIMEOUT=10.0       # seconds for a new connection
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__STATEMENT_TIMEOUT=30.0     # server-side per-statement cap (s)
# QUERYSHIELD_DATABASE__SSLMODE=require            # disable|allow|prefer|require|verify-ca|verify-full

# ---- Application ----
# Log verbosity for QueryShield's own logging (CRITICAL|ERROR|WARNING|INFO|DEBUG).
# QUERYSHIELD_LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# ---- Optional YAML config file ----
# Absolute or relative path to a YAML file whose values sit BELOW environment
# variables in precedence. Supports ${VAR} interpolation from the environment
# (an undefined ${VAR} fails closed). Unset means "no file".
# QUERYSHIELD_CONFIG_FILE=./queryshield.yaml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration tests only
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Point this at a DISPOSABLE PostgreSQL to run `pytest -m integration`. When
# unset, the integration tests skip. It is deliberately separate from the app
# database URL above and is ignored by the application config loader.
# QUERYSHIELD_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://queryshield_test:queryshield_test@localhost:5432/queryshield_test

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT yet implemented (documented for later phases; currently ignored)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ---- LLM (Mistral, hosted API only; see ADR-0009) ----
# MISTRAL_API_KEY=your-mistral-api-key-here
# MISTRAL_MODEL=mistral-large-latest
# ---- Cache (optional; see ADR-0007) ----
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
